[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3022904626","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108152#issuecomment-3022904626","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108152","id":3022904626,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60Ld0y","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-01T09:18:32Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T09:18:32Z","body":"This is a hard limit, see:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e1b4101e3460dd9c6ba0b7f8d88e9751b8383f5b/core/object/object.cpp#L2408\n\nThis is pretty much unavoidable without breaking changes, 16 million objects is a pretty permissive limit, I'd say the solution here is to avoid it, this many objects will be taking up a pretty high amount of memory anyway, even a low estimate of the size of a plain `Object` means that takes at least 2-4 GB of memory even without overhead \n\nThis should be documented better though ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3022904626/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024957963","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108152#issuecomment-3024957963","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108152","id":3024957963,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60TTIL","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-01T17:37:59Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T17:37:59Z","body":"I do have a WIP `ObjectDB` replacement that I'm working on for 3.x that could *potentially* be forward ported. It defaults to allowing full 32 bit range (i.e. 4 billion simultaneous), but I have to convert 3.x `ObjectID` fully to 64 bit first, Godot 3.x has some bugs where 32 bit intermediates are used.\n\nHaving said that I agree with @AThousandShips , if you are storing a lot of data, then this should be arrays within godot objects, rather than arrays _of_ godot objects, as the latter is never going to work fast or be good on memory use / cache. Of course this may be difficult in bound languages in some situations.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024957963/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024972837","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108152#issuecomment-3024972837","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108152","id":3024972837,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60TWwl","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-01T17:43:25Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T17:43:25Z","body":"How have you implemented the validators with a smaller range? Or are you skipping that safety step?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024972837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024995021","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108152#issuecomment-3024995021","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108152","id":3024995021,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60TcLN","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-01T17:51:16Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T17:51:16Z","body":"> How have you implemented the validators with a smaller range? Or are you skipping that safety step?\n\n32 bit ID, 32 bit revision, 64 bits in total. Each individual instance ID would have to rollover 4 billion times to get the possibility of a duplicate.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024995021/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3025001904","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108152#issuecomment-3025001904","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108152","id":3025001904,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60Td2w","user":{"login":"EclipsedStar0","id":83985361,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzOTg1MzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83985361?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0","html_url":"https://github.com/EclipsedStar0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EclipsedStar0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-01T17:53:55Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T17:53:55Z","body":"Alright, good to know that it’s a hard limit. Thanks for taking the time to look at it. I’ll probably do what @lawnjelly suggested and store more info in the objects themselves instead of making new objects.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3025001904/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3032931503","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108152#issuecomment-3032931503","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108152","id":3032931503,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60xtyv","user":{"login":"Adrenesis","id":11399943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzk5OTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11399943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis","html_url":"https://github.com/Adrenesis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adrenesis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T16:50:51Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T17:29:27Z","body":"This is way more important than it seems and for totally different reasons. Godot has currently no way of debugging which instance ids are used and if you try \"is_instance_id_valid()\" on random ids, Godot will then spam this crash condition for absolutely no reasons:\n\n [godot/core/object/object.h](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/49a5bc7b616bd04689a2c89e89bda41f50241464/core/object/object.h#L1048)\n\nWhat I used to do back in the Godot 3 days is something similar to what today would look like this:\n\n```\nfor i in range(1000000):\n\tif is_instance_id_valid(i):\n\t\tvar obj : Object = instance_from_id(i)\n\t\tif is_instance_valid(obj):\n\t\t\tprint(\"%d: %d\" % [i, obj.get_class()])\n```\nThen save it in a log, then compare multiple instance of those with a diff software to know if the memory used after an action is justified or not...\n\nSadly enough, Godot IDs are way too big now to use that kind of scam. I didn't find any issue on the subject which means I'm one of the last developers to actually check a memory map for actual memory leaks - **not the one you think are there, but the one you can observe**.\n\nAre we becoming like those POE2 devs who are not even able to debug the damage in their own game, because even the devs don't have the tools for it? **Are we just random code typers with absolutly no ideas of how the memory is used? the question to me is still there and very important.**\n\nI'm working on a Tower Defense with strong Data-Oriented-Designed optimizations, and still at each wave, my game is generating hundreds of Godot Objects, which I can see in the Debugger.... but where is the tool to know what are those objects? Are those simple `InputEventKey` or some unmanaged `Texture`, I don't know and I have no way to know.\n\n**Seriously, why Godot has still no way to check the memory map of a game? where is the function `get_used_instance_ids()` in the `@GlobalScope`?**\n\nAfter 9 years of using Godot (I do since the version 2.1.1), Godot has fell in the pitfall trap that Unity first did, and I stopped using Unity exactly for this reason. If Godot is intended to be used for making games, I'll tell you after 20 years of video-game development, that making games is about knowing what is going on in your memory. I'm not supposed to beat around the bush for hours and make big theories of what is using the memory, it should just be displayed somewhere!\n\nHow come the fact, that somewhere between Godot 3.x and 4.x someone changed the max_slot and the instance id generation for random ids without thinking about that? Are those people just praying for memory leak to not happen in their projects?\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3032931503/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3032991991","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108152#issuecomment-3032991991","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108152","id":3032991991,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60x8j3","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T17:13:46Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T17:29:22Z","body":"That crash condition will not fire because of `is_instance_id_valid`, you're looking at the wrong method, what are you basing this on?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3032991991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart"